{
  "id": "21525_hajirau",
  "headword": "{恥|は}じらう",
  "reading": "はじらう",
  "romaji": "hajirau",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be bashful; to feel shy; to be coy",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be bashful; to feel shy; to be coy",
      "explanation": "To show shyness or embarrassment, often in a charming or endearing way. Implies a mild, gentle form of embarrassment rather than intense shame."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21525_hajirau_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{恥|は}じらって{目|め}をそらした。",
      "english": "She shyly looked away.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21525_hajirau_ex2",
      "japanese": "{褒|ほ}められると{恥|は}じらう{様子|ようす}がかわいい。",
      "english": "The way they get bashful when complimented is cute.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21525_hajirau_ex3",
      "japanese": "{恥|は}じらいながら{花束|はなたば}を{受|う}け{取|と}った。",
      "english": "They bashfully accepted the bouquet.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A godan verb derived from {恥|は}じる (to feel ashamed). While {恥|は}じる has a broader meaning covering genuine shame, {恥|は}じらう specifically suggests gentle shyness or coyness — often perceived as charming or endearing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {恥|は}じらいを{見|み}せる: to show bashfulness\n- {恥|は}じらいもなく: without any shame, shamelessly\n- {恥|は}じらう{姿|すがた}: a bashful figure\n- {恥|は}じらいながら: bashfully, while being shy\n\nNOMINAL FORM:\nThe noun form {恥|は}じらい is frequently used on its own:\n- {恥|は}じらい: bashfulness, shyness, coyness\n- {乙女|おとめ}の{恥|は}じらい: a maiden's bashfulness\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {恥|は}じる: to feel ashamed — covers stronger feelings of shame\n- {恥|は}ずかしがる: to act embarrassed — focuses on the outward behavior\n- {照|て}れる: to be embarrassed, flustered — more casual and everyday",
